  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "From the state Housing Element Annual Progress Report, through 2025.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001101",
        "SRC-001110"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CTCAC CA-26-436: Camino Commons, located at 96 West El Camino Real in Mountain View on a 0.87 acre site, requested $3,668,820 in annual federal tax credits and $9,665,896 in total state tax credits but is being recommended for $3,668,820 in annual federal tax credits and $9,665,895 in total state tax credits and $23,650,730 of tax- exempt bond cap to finance the new construction of 79 units of housing, consisting of 78 restricted rental units and 1 unrestricted manager's unit.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001675"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Earlier project name in the February 2023 city project summary: West El Camino Family Apartments. The site held the Cusimano Family Colonial Mortuary since the 1960s.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003230",
        "SRC-003228"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "City funding of $8 million is $1.26 million in state PLHA funds plus $6.74 million in Housing Impact Fees, as a construction/permanent loan at 3% simple interest with no payments during construction. County funding is $7.9 million under the City-County Measure A MOU.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003231"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "September 2026 council report: the state awarded $46,354,095 in low-income housing tax credits and $23,650,730 in tax-exempt bond allocation; the TEFRA authorization is up to $50 million, with about $24 million of bonds expected to be issued by CMFA.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003231"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Under the Measure A MOU the city is to acquire the land and ground lease it to the developer; a Danco spokesperson told the Mountain View Voice the lease is $1 per year for 99 years.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003226",
        "SRC-003228"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CTCAC staff report: 12 units (15%) receive HUD Section 8 project-based vouchers; CDLAC analyst Sarah Lester, CTCAC analyst Cynthia Compton.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001675"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "February 2023 anticipated permanent sources totaled $78,715,705: bank loan $15,151,494, County $6,984,000, City $8,000,000, HCD MHP or IIG $17,451,750, tax credit equity $29,218,461, other $2,000,000. The council report text cites a County request of $6,894,000.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003230",
        "SRC-003226"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Danco's project page names Housing Trust Silicon Valley for predevelopment and permanent funding and Mountain View housing funds in the financing plan.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003229"
      ]
    }
  ],
